Tue Oct 27 18:39:31 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.1.0:
  * hooks: opt-in wrapping of fish scripts as rtk run --shell fish,
    integrity verification for rewritten commands
  * ng: compact Angular build tables safely
  * cli: -h, --help and help are now handed to the wrapped tool
  * permissions: fail closed on unreadable settings, match deny
    and ask rules past assignments and wrappers
  * pytest: keep error and failure lines, locations and setup
    errors in summaries; cargo keeps slow-test counts for nextest
  * gain: exclude zero-input rows from exec time totals; recall
    uses a 64-bit content hash so colliding outputs are kept
  * hook, init, discover, json and js fixes, including leaving git
    unrewritten in Claude Code managed worktrees, and more compact
    Ruff and SQLFluff output
- Refresh the vendored dependencies (243 crates); licence tag gains
  Zlib (foldhash, linked via rusqlite and ratatui)
- rtk-unbundle-sqlite.patch and rtk-no-deny-warnings.patch
  still apply unchanged (upstream still bundles sqlite and
  denies warnings)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Oct 15 04:44:21 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.0.1 (major 0.x -> 1.x):
  * BREAKING: rtk proxy is now rtk bypass (old name stays as alias),
    --ultra-compact is removed, rtk gain excludes oversized outputs
    from its headline rate
  * BREAKING: upstream splits a BUSL-1.1 compression engine out of the
    Apache-2.0 CLI; this package builds the Apache-2.0 rtk-oss edition
    with --no-default-features, so no BUSL code is shipped and pipelines
    stay inert as before
  * New pipeline engine with CLI pipelines, hook gate and llm-proxy,
    plus the rtk-proxy daemon (not packaged) and agent plugin routing
  * hook: support OpenCode V2, Desktop and Windows, judge OpenCode
    against its own permission rules, close permission-gate holes in
    command segmentation; init fails closed on a missing .claude dir
  * rewrite: rewrite inner commands of quoted sh/bash/zsh/fish -c wrappers
  * 0.52.0 fixes across ast-grep, curl stdin, diff usage errors, gh/glab
    tokenizing, go test summaries, ls tokenizing, mvn goals, pytest ANSI
    handling and tracking; 1.0.1 fixes gain pipeline-share hints and
    RTK_PROXY_BIND handling
  * many more fixes; see upstream's release notes for the full list
- Rebase rtk-unbundle-sqlite.patch for rusqlite 0.31 -> 0.34 (still needed,
  upstream keeps bundling as default), including the Cargo.lock hunk that drops
  the libsqlite3-sys cc edge so --locked cargo builds pass;
  rtk-no-deny-warnings.patch still applies
- Refresh the vendored dependencies (243 crates); no licence change on the
  Apache-2.0 build graph
- BuildRequires curl: the new curl stdin test shells out to the real curl
  binary

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Oct  3 05:43:59 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.51.0:
  * BREAKING: rtk run/err/test/summary execute the wrapped program
    directly instead of rebuilding the positional arguments into
    one string for sh -c, so globs, variables and operators are no
    longer expanded by an unrequested shell; pass a script
    explicitly, e.g. rtk test --shell sh 'cargo test'. A missing
    program now exits 127 through the runners' own failure path
  * search: a bare file list (-l/-L/--files) folds the directory
    prefix all paths share into a one-line header and prints only
    the tails, losslessly; non-path lines pass through verbatim
  * hook: native Google Antigravity plugin lifecycle and hook
    support
  * cli: a program that cannot be run answers 126 as sh does, 127
    stays for a missing one; unresolvable single-string commands go
    through the platform shell
  * read: track Python triple-quoted strings; pytest: keep the
    elapsed duration; pip: stop doubling the tool name
  * discover: name zero-session scans, case-insensitive Windows
    project filter, token boundaries for rewrite rules
  * diff: unreadable files exit 2; ruff: bypass never_worse only
    for rtk-injected output; init: --agent cursor installs Cursor
    only
  * many more fixes; see upstream's release notes for the full list
- Refresh the vendored dependencies; no licence change
- BuildRequires jq: the new hook decision test runs
  hooks/claude/rtk-rewrite.sh, which needs jq at build time

